  "result": "The 30-minute lesson on O3 is written, with a short quiz and its key. I didn't take the quiz and couldn't count the lesson's words. The word-count commands were blocked, so I'm estimating about 3,100, which is inside the 2,700–6,750 range for a 30-minute lesson.\n\n**Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`\n\nIt starts from a helper with one desk, which maps to the context window. It then covers:\n- why the program re-sends the whole context on every step, which makes cost grow faster than the number of steps\n- why nothing survives between sessions unless you save it\n- retrieval for finding the right manual passage, and notes for facts like a student's training status\n\nThe win is that you can decide, for each piece of information in the makerspace assistant, whether it goes in the context, in saved notes, or in a document that is retrieved only when needed. It has three figures, practice checks with immediate feedback, and a worked example sorting the assistant's information into those three places. It cites Anthropic's context-engineering post and the Claude docs, and I fetched those pages in this session.\n\n**Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items. The key is `keys/0002.json`, and I'm not putting any answers in this message.\n\nI also created `RESOURCES.md` with the three sources and added a line to `NOTES.md` saying the lesson and quiz are ready. I didn't write a cheat sheet or a learning record, because you haven't shown any new understanding yet.\n\nQuestion for you: do you want a community to test your design with, such as a forum or a class? `RESOURCES.md` has no community yet, and I didn't want to guess.\n\nYou can ask me anything about the lesson in the chat, and say when you want to take the quiz.",
